Hi Shengli,

I am a little confused about the following words on how to calculate the p-value of DMR:

Based on the refined regions, we calculated

the significance of the regions by combining the

p-values of DMCs within that region. We used the

dependence adjustment of the Stouffer-Liptak test to

combine p-values [22,23].

For some CpG, the low-p is because case has lower methylation rate than control, however, for some other CpGs, the case has higher methylation rate. If we only combine the p-value, how can we know in this region, it is significant? For example, for a 10 cpgs region, 5 have higher methylation rate, 5 have lower methylation rate for case, the result should be canceled if we consider the region. But if you combine the CpG p value, it will be significant. Did you consider the direction of significant in your software?  Thanks!

Gengsheng

